Graph dependencies

These patches apply to the pinned official npm packages during postinstall.
They change the ESM modules used by the explorer's Rollup build and their types.

3d-force-graph: exposes nodesPerStack and passes numDimensions to the renderer.
three-forcegraph: preserves stacked levels, size-based spacing, depthOverride,
dagIgnore, and world names in cycle errors. Stack sizes are grouped in one pass.
three-render-objects: preserves the orthographic camera used for 2D mode.

Three.js 0.162.0 is the last release with WebGL1 support. The renderer stays on
1.29.5 because 1.30.0 imports the newer Three.js WebGPU module, even in WebGL mode.

Run npm ci to install and apply the patches, then npm run compile to rebuild.
When upgrading a patched package, update its pinned version and patch together.
